WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.935
From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.403
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:06.039
between Popeyes in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.374
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.147
The fountain drinks at
Popeyes come in three sizes.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.316
The small, which is 22 ounces,

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.852
the medium, which is 30 ounces,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:23.690
and the large, which is,
of course, 40 ounces.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.458
40 ounces.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.961
That's so much soda.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.963
In the UK, drinks only come in two sizes,

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.232
as a kids size or as a regular size.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.700
We're not sure how much
is in either of these,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.235
so we're going to measure them both.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.903
A little over 300.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.610
About 450.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.749
But those aren't the biggest, I say!

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.151
Actually, at the Popeyes in the US,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.887
you can also get a gallon of sweet tea

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.456
and unsweetened tea.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:01:00.226
One whole gallon.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.828
Ah, look at this!

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.563
Gallon, gallon.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.899
Oh, and don't you hate
when dummies do that thing

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.733
where they're like,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.836
"Hey, the medium is the
same size as the large!"

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.805
And it never is, it's a total con, so.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.706
Medium soda, large cup.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.913
Oh, wow, guys!

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.548
The medium's about the
same size as the large,

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.783
except for, like, oh, I
don't know, 10 ounces!

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.218
Dumb TikTokers. You guys aren't even ...

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.087
out-of-your-league TikTokers.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.523
I'm the fast-food king online! All right?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.395
When was this cleaned last?

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:42.569
Ooh,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.571
I'm gonna go 36. What do you think?

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.639
I mean, it could have been
the amount to top of this cup,

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.609
but again, you can't
fill this to the brim.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.844
You have to put a cap on it.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.246
In the UK, fries just
come as a regular serving.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.716
US, we got two Popeyes fries sizes,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.784
a regular and a large.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.519
The regular, as we have here,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.888
just came with the side of
the three-piece we got here,

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.223
and of course a large,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.626
which is a box of just fries.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.594
Harry: We're going to weigh these to see

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.162
how they compare to the US.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.730
Joe: We, of course, now are going to also

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.299
weigh our largest fry.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.139
Do not sleep on these fries.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:20.640
You'll be surprised to learn

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.110
that the inside of this
scale is disgusting.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.745
A Popeyes chicken sandwich in the UK

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.649
weighs exactly 250 grams.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.784
Joe: In the US, it weighs

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.355
270 grams.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.557
In the US, Popeyes signature chicken

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.692
comes in seven serving sizes.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.627
We'll start with these.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.762
So, of course, the one-piece kids meal,

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.599
then you can upgrade to
a two-piece regular meal,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.801
which comes with a side and a biscuit,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.904
or you can get yourself the three-piece,

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:54.307
and a four-piece. Side and a biscuit.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.909
From there, you can get yourself

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.977
an eight-piece family meal,

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.914
the 12-piece for the family as well,

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.949
or just for one person over a weekend,

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:06.386
and the largest, the 16-piece.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.453
Are you kidding me?

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.454
[laughs]

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.591
How absurd is this? Look
at all this chicken.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.159
In the UK, the signature chicken comes

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.494
as a two-piece meal,

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.828
as a three-piece meal,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.263
as a six-piece sharer,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.531
as a nine-piece sharer,

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.900
or our largest size, the 12-piece sharer.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.502
Let's weigh a wing, a thigh, and a leg

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.137
to see whose chickens are bigger.

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.540
So, in the UK, our thigh,
leg, and wing combo

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.509
came to around 290 grams.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.214
Here we go. First guy up, the leg.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.050
Next up, got that wing.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.117
Kind of a wimpy-looking one.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.119
And this one, the thigh.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.860
How 'bout the tendies?

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.230
In the US, we have these following sizes:

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.898
A kids meal has a one-piece,

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:55.268
but what's up? They gave us two!

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:56.869
And then from there you get a three-piece,

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.037
which they forgot,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.174
and then we have five-piece,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.308
comes with a side and a biscuit,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.243
eight pieces.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.578
I feel like they're getting
bigger as I go along.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:06.980
Look at the size of this tender.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.649
Then we have the 12-piece.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.284
I mean, guys, this is like a --

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:12.285
look at this!

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.686
Did you know they're this big?

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.189
This is fantastic. I
love how big these are.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.424
That's what I'm talking
about, Popeyes! Thank you.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.060
And, of course, the 16-piece.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.395
Look at this bad boy.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.130
Look at the size of these guys.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.633
Tenders in the UK come
in four portion sizes,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.568
as a two-piece, which is the kids meal,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:32.772
as a three-piece, a
five-piece, and an eight-piece.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.140
Next up is the nuggets.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.908
These can be found in servings of

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.510
a four-piece kids meal,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.145
a six-piece kids meal,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.280
eight-piece,

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.914
the 12-piece,

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.616
24-piece,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.218
36 pieces,

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.054
and then this double pile right here,

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:50.990
the biggest order, 48 pieces.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.793
And I have to say, does
not look like enough.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:57.730
I know I could destroy that
48-piece with confidence.

00:04:58.665 --> 00:04:59.499
What do we got here?

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.768
Oh, look at this sticker! This is fun.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.202
Yeah, look at these guys!

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.804
Look at this big one playing a saxophone,

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.472
how fun is that?

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.573
That's cool, right?

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.309
In the UK, we actually
call our nuggets bites,

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.810
and they come in the following sizes:

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.445
There's a four-piece,
which is a kids meal,

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.081
a six-piece, a nine-piece, and a 12-piece.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.683
Unfortunately, we
couldn't get these today.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.985
USA, we got biscuits, baby.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.154
These are the not-cookie biscuits

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.189
that have come up before in
other "Food Wars" episodes.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.191
These are the biscuits biscuits,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.860
and at Popeyes, you can get them in one,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.430
either on its own or probably
with just about every meal.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.832
You can also get them in six.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.400
It's, like, rolling right down here.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.636
And you can also get them in 12.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.571
Just overflowing biscuits over here.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.674
We actually do have biscuits
on the UK Popeyes menu.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:44.110
If you order it as a
side, you get one biscuit.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.847
The biggest single item you
can get on the US Popeyes menu

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:50.450
is this, the Bigger Family Feast.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.419
It comes with 12 pieces of chicken,

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.787
five chicken sandwiches,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:58.524
two large sides, got the
slaw and the mashed potatoes,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.761
five biscuits, and five apple pies.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.630
This entire thing will set
you back about 60 bucks

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.000
and clocks in at 10,000 calories

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.303
if you choose a more calorific
side, like the fries.

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.604
I did not.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.373
That pretty much dwarfs
our largest single item,

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.074
which is this, the 12-piece sharer.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:17.643
You get 12 pieces of
chicken, four regular sides,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.412
four biscuits, and four drinks,

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.914
all for the price of
24 pounds and 95 pence,

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.017
which was around $33.50
at the time of recording.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:28.821
Mm.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.456
We're so bad at fried chicken in the UK.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.125
We just don't do it well.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.727
But this, I gotta say,

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.263
I feel like a certain Kentucky-based chain

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.598
has had the monopoly for far too long,

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.599
and they've let their standards slip.

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:41.100
So this is really good.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.135
I'm thrilled that the standards

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.836
are hopefully going to get raised.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.343
And here's everything you
can find at a US Popeyes

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.612
you won't find in the UK.

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.913
And here are most of
the things you'll find

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.215
at a UK Popeyes that you
won't find in the US.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.083
Let's start with the chicken.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.786
There are two main exclusive
chicken options in the UK.

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:03.022
Firstly in the UK, we can get
a chicken sandwich deluxe.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.290
It's just a Popeyes chicken sandwich,

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.626
but there's cheese and
lettuce on here as well.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.429
What he means to say

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.930
is they took a delicious chicken sandwich

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.132
and added a bunch of junk.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:15.635
Deluxe means vegetables,

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:19.405
aka the junk I don't want on
my crispy chicken sandwich.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.307
Popeyes in the UK also sell hot wings.

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:25.978
These come in orders of
three, five, eight, 12, or 20.

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:27.280
Now, it might surprise
some American viewers,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.247
but London in particular

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:29.749
has a pretty big chicken-shop culture,

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.484
and we're pretty passionate
about our hot wings,

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.119
so let's see how these measure up.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.520
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.924
Don't get it twisted.
We're the wings country,

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.025
and we should have those.

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:40.960
I have no idea why we don't have those.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:46.265
That to me is a very good chicken wing.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.301
Good level of heat, very
crispy on the outside,

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.670
very juicy on the inside,
what more can you want?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.473
We only have one exclusive chicken item.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:54.474
Well, it's technically not an item,

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:55.942
it's more of a style of chicken.

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.009
Both in the US and the UK,

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:58.711
they have the spicy and
they have the regular,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.647
but we also have something
called the blackened chicken.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:04.016
It is a chicken option without breading,

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.718
therefore, who cares?

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:07.954
And it comes in the form
of sandwich or tenders.

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:10.389
Here it is, blackened chicken.

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.592
It's called fried chicken for a reason.

00:08:12.592 --> 00:08:15.027
This is just, like, cooked on a grill?

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:17.463
Grilled chicken at Popeyes.

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.131
What is wrong with you?

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.435
Oh.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:23.503
Nope.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:24.537
In both the UK and the US,

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:25.771
Popeyes chicken sandwiches,

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.273
fried chicken, and chicken tenders

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:29.342
are available as either classic or spicy.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.410
One interesting fact is that
someone from Popeyes told us

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.613
that the UK version of the spicy chicken

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:35.648
is actually hotter than it is in America,

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:37.216
after they tried it on some focus groups

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:39.352
and they kept asking them
to crank up the heat.

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:41.654
Who said British people
can't handle spices, huh?

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:46.859
Now, this is not an exclusive

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.160
because it's available in both countries.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.562
However, this is my first time

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.697
trying an American-style biscuit.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:52.965
Now, the obvious statement is that, to me,

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.667
this just looks like a scone.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.602
The color is there, the shape is there,

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:58.838
the kind of flaky layers are there.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.072
It even kind of smells like a scone.

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.941
And the fact that this is
being served with fried chicken

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:04.644
to me and to I think most
British people is really weird.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.749
Don't get me wrong, this is tasty,

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:11.417
I'm just still struggling
to see any differences

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.286
between this and a British scone.

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:15.421
Popeyes in the US doesn't
just serve chicken,

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:17.323
it also has seafood,

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.125
something you can't
find in the UK Popeyes.

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.394
Now, the US Popeyes did for a while

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.062
have a Cajun flounder sandwich,

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:25.765
which is a fried flounder fillet in a bun

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:27.600
with some pickles and tartar sauce.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.802
At the recording of this,
it is no longer available.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:31.070
I don't know if it was
a limited-time thing

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.172
or they just stopped, they're
taking a break, I don't know.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:34.941
But you can still get the popcorn shrimp.

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:36.008
This is it.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:40.346
And it comes in a quarter-pound serving.

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:41.714
There are no seafood options in the UK,

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:43.015
but we do have one vegan option

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.183
which you guys don't have in the US,

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:45.985
and that's the Creole red bean sandwich.

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:48.087
This is a 100% plant-based red bean patty

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:50.289
with some tomato, some
lettuce, and a Creole sauce,

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:52.325
but unfortunately we weren't
able to get one today.

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.626
I will say the Popeyes menu in the US

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:55.261
doesn't look very vegetarian-friendly,

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.662
so maybe if this takes off in the UK,

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:57.964
you guys can get it too.

00:09:57.964 --> 00:09:59.265
Whatever the hell that thing is,

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:02.802
100% plant-based red bean pat -- ugh.

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:04.937
That will never touch American shores.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.707
That can stay in the UK.

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:11.043
No one's going to Popeyes for
vegetarian, vegan anything.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:13.245
It's a fried-chicken place. So no.

00:10:13.245 --> 00:10:15.681
Now, we have two sides that
are exclusive to the US.

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.183
Red beans and rice.

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:18.084
Grr!

00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:21.520
Oh, do we got a bad boy? A thingy-thing?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.123
Did they not give us any silverware?

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:27.393
Mystery spoon from somewhere
in the office, all right.

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:30.129
Red beans and rice, there it is.

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.598
And coleslaw.

00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:34.300
We just have the one
exclusive side in the UK,

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.167
and it's onion rings.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.402
These are battered using buttermilk,

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:37.703
similarly to the chicken.

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:39.939
Unfortunately, we weren't able
to get these today either.

00:10:39.939 --> 00:10:41.741
I got a bunch of sauces in front of me,

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:44.110
and you know what that means! It's:

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.745
Sauce Talk.

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:48.648
We've got a tartar sauce.

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:51.517
The Creole cocktail sauce.

00:10:51.517 --> 00:10:55.621
Creole is a type of cuisine in Louisiana.

00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:57.723
Blackened ranch.

00:10:57.723 --> 00:10:59.091
Was this supposed to be
for the blackened chicken,

00:10:59.091 --> 00:10:59.959
do you think?

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:02.762
And of course we have
regular buttermilk ranch.

00:11:02.762 --> 00:11:04.563
Well, we already know what ranch is.

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:07.199
Ranchy.

00:11:07.199 --> 00:11:08.434
Blackened ranch.

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:12.171
Oh, that's way better.

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:13.873
The sweet heat.

00:11:13.873 --> 00:11:15.274
Had this earlier with the tenders,

00:11:15.274 --> 00:11:17.309
can confirm, fantastic sauce.

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:19.445
Wild honey mustard

00:11:19.445 --> 00:11:22.682
and the bayou Buffalo sauce.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:25.317
In the UK, we have the
following exclusive sauces:

00:11:25.317 --> 00:11:27.520
we have this voodoo sweet chili sauce,

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.423
which could be quite similar
to the US's sweet heat sauce.

00:11:30.423 --> 00:11:32.258
Then we have a garlic mayo

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:33.959
as well as a mango habanero sauce,

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:35.127
which sounds really good.

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:35.961
It's not an exclusive,

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:37.363
but shout-out to the Mardi Gras mustard,

00:11:37.363 --> 00:11:39.131
because this stuff slaps.

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:43.636
Now, it's not exactly an exclusive,

00:11:43.636 --> 00:11:44.603
but it's worth a shout-out.

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:47.039
Musician Megan Thee Stallion

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:49.008
recently launched a collab with Popeyes

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:50.543
and released the Hottie Sauce.

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:52.078
You can get it as a side for dip

00:11:52.078 --> 00:11:53.579
or pre-add it to your chicken sandwich.

00:11:53.579 --> 00:11:54.413
Or if you're in the UK,

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:56.182
you can dip a hot wing
into the Hottie Sauce

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:57.349
and have a hot wing summer.

00:11:58.217 --> 00:12:00.586
She's also becoming a Popeyes franchisee,

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:03.155
as she is opening her own Popeyes soon.

00:12:03.155 --> 00:12:05.057
And then underneath this, it says,

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:08.661
"Need some 'WAP' content
here, open to ideas."

00:12:08.661 --> 00:12:11.097
I'm assuming she is the
one who did the song "WAP"?

00:12:11.097 --> 00:12:12.164
I don't know who this person is.

00:12:12.164 --> 00:12:13.966
I've never heard "WAP."

00:12:13.966 --> 00:12:16.035
I just know it as a
reference on the internet.

00:12:17.737 --> 00:12:20.573
And I am going to bask in the glory

00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:22.007
that only some my age can,

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:25.311
of not having any idea
what a popular thing is.

00:12:25.311 --> 00:12:26.412
Ah.

00:12:26.412 --> 00:12:27.646
Desserts!

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:31.117
This is a cinnamon apple pie.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.223
Oh, my God [mumbles].

00:12:37.223 --> 00:12:38.023
What?

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:39.158
And ...

00:12:39.158 --> 00:12:39.992
ugh!

00:12:42.094 --> 00:12:44.363
Chocolate chip cookies.

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:46.198
Was she with Paul Davis,

00:12:46.198 --> 00:12:47.867
Pete Davidson for
awhile? Was that the one?

00:12:49.301 --> 00:12:50.936
We have an exclusive
dessert option of our own,

00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:52.204
which is ice cream sundaes.

00:12:52.204 --> 00:12:54.406
Now, these are available
in the following flavors:

00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:57.676
vanilla, chocolate, caramel,

00:12:57.676 --> 00:13:00.079
with Oreos, or with Lotus Biscoff.

00:13:00.079 --> 00:13:01.447
You can also pay an extra 50 pence

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:03.149
to add little pieces of Oreo or Biscoff

00:13:03.149 --> 00:13:04.316
to any of these sundaes.

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:05.451
If you've watched "Food
Wars" for long enough,

00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:07.319
you'll know that I really
don't like Biscoff,

00:13:07.319 --> 00:13:08.854
and I know that's a very
controversial opinion,

00:13:08.854 --> 00:13:10.856
so don't send for me, please.

00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:12.925
All right, so before you saw
those big gallons of tea.

00:13:12.925 --> 00:13:15.961
There was sweet tea and
unsweetened tea. Very nice.

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:18.597
We also have a premium lemonade.
That's this right here.

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:21.167
I've been sipping on because
this chicken is getting to me.

00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:24.270
They also have premium
strawberry lemonade,

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.840
and they also have this
right here, Hawaiian Punch.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.341
You guys don't know
what Hawaiian Punch is?

00:13:29.341 --> 00:13:31.443
It is fruit punch.

00:13:33.913 --> 00:13:36.348
Oh, yeah, all the good
stuff's at the bottom.

00:13:36.348 --> 00:13:39.451
And ginger ale. Ugh, I have
a headache all of a sudden.

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.053
We have a range of
exclusive drinks in the UK,

00:13:41.053 --> 00:13:42.755
some of which are hot and
some of which are cold.

00:13:42.755 --> 00:13:43.756
We'll start with the hot drinks.

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:45.124
It wouldn't be a British fast-food menu

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:46.592
unless you could get a cup of tea.

00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:47.893
Then we have a range of hot coffees,

00:13:47.893 --> 00:13:50.563
including a cappuccino, an Americano,

00:13:50.563 --> 00:13:52.131
a flat white, and a latte.

00:13:52.131 --> 00:13:53.032
Then we're on to the cold drinks,

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:54.133
including some bottled options,

00:13:54.133 --> 00:13:55.668
like this Oasis summer fruits,

00:13:55.668 --> 00:13:58.871
this sparkling water, and
this orange Capri Sun.

00:13:58.871 --> 00:13:59.905
Of all the linguistic differences

00:13:59.905 --> 00:14:00.940
between the States and the UK,

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.508
this might be the one
that annoys me the most.

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:05.544
We pronounce this CAP-ri Sun.
You pronounce it Cap-RI Sun.

00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:06.378
You're putting the emphasis

00:14:06.378 --> 00:14:08.881
on the completely wrong part
of the word. Get it right.

00:14:08.881 --> 00:14:10.049
In the UK, you can also get a range

00:14:10.049 --> 00:14:11.183
of hand-spun milkshakes,

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:12.885
which unfortunately we couldn't get today.

00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:13.719
When they are available,

00:14:13.719 --> 00:14:15.421
you can get them in similar
flavors to the sundaes.

00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:18.791
They come as Biscoff,
Oreo, vanilla, chocolate,

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:20.392
caramel, or also strawberry.

00:14:20.392 --> 00:14:21.227
And just like the sundaes,

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:22.461
you can pay an additional 50 pence

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:24.597
for an additional Biscoff or Oreo topping.

00:14:27.366 --> 00:14:28.934
The chicken sandwich from a UK Popeyes

00:14:28.934 --> 00:14:30.069
contains the following.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.405
If you get the chicken
sandwich at a US Popeyes,

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:35.407
it contains this.

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:36.342
What if you made it a meal?

00:14:36.342 --> 00:14:39.478
You add the regular serving
of Popeyes Cajun fries,

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.513
you'll be adding the following.

00:14:41.513 --> 00:14:43.883
A side of fries in the UK
contains the following.

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:47.353
Poof!

00:14:47.353 --> 00:14:49.088
Add this medium Coke to the mix,

00:14:49.088 --> 00:14:51.390
and you're adding 368 calories,

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.726
99 carbs, all of those are sugar,

00:14:53.726 --> 00:14:55.895
and 88 milligrams of sodium.

00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:59.198
And a regular Coke in
the UK adds 180 calories,

00:14:59.198 --> 00:15:01.300
zero grams of fat or saturated fat,

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.036
45.6 grams of carbs,
all of which are sugars,

00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:05.337
and zero sodium.

00:15:05.337 --> 00:15:07.273
And what is the total of this US meal?

00:15:07.273 --> 00:15:10.643
1,335 calories,

00:15:10.643 --> 00:15:12.578
56 grams of total fat,

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.914
19 of those grams are saturated fat,

00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:17.216
182 grams of carbs,

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:19.952
106.5 of those grams of sugar,

00:15:19.952 --> 00:15:23.722
and 2,118 milligrams of sodium.

00:15:23.722 --> 00:15:25.424
Yo.

00:15:25.424 --> 00:15:26.592
The UK total:

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:27.960
1,300 calories,

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.495
63.7 grams of fat,

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:31.630
of which 20.4 grams of saturated,

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.699
135.4 grams of carbs,

00:15:33.699 --> 00:15:35.834
of which 54.8 grams are sugars,

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:38.504
and 1,160 milligrams of sodium.

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:40.506
Obviously the sugar stats here look bad,

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:41.774
but in Popeyes' defense,

00:15:41.774 --> 00:15:43.742
a majority of the sugar is coming from

00:15:43.742 --> 00:15:46.045
this 30 ounces -- [chuckles] 30 ounces --

00:15:46.045 --> 00:15:47.012
of Coca-Cola.

00:15:47.012 --> 00:15:48.914
Now, if you got a sugar-free soda instead,

00:15:48.914 --> 00:15:50.349
it would be a much lower figure.

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:52.151
The meal does contain, however,

00:15:52.151 --> 00:15:55.054
95% of your daily saturated fat

00:15:55.054 --> 00:15:58.357
as well as 92% of your daily sodium.

00:15:58.357 --> 00:15:59.792
Perhaps surprisingly, it seems as if

00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:01.493
the fat and saturated fat totals

00:16:01.493 --> 00:16:03.796
are actually higher in the
UK than they are in the US.

00:16:03.796 --> 00:16:05.631
This meal would take you just over 100%

00:16:05.631 --> 00:16:07.766
of your daily saturated fat allowance.

00:16:07.766 --> 00:16:10.536
However, the sodium
content is way higher here

00:16:10.536 --> 00:16:11.704
than it is in the UK.

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:13.605
The biggest difference comes
in the chicken sandwich.

00:16:13.605 --> 00:16:15.908
This guy right here, for some reason,

00:16:15.908 --> 00:16:20.713
has 260% more sodium than that in the UK.

00:16:23.983 --> 00:16:26.118
Unfortunately, Popeyes has not disclosed

00:16:26.118 --> 00:16:29.288
a full ingredients list
in the US, only allergens.

00:16:29.288 --> 00:16:30.589
It's a similar deal in the UK.

00:16:30.589 --> 00:16:32.458
Popeyes doesn't disclose
a full ingredients list,

00:16:32.458 --> 00:16:33.425
just allergens.

00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:35.627
The only sort of surprising
thing we found out in the US

00:16:35.627 --> 00:16:38.530
is that there is fish present
in the beans and rice.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.300
But what else do we know
about the Popeyes food?

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.134
Ah!

00:16:42.134 --> 00:16:43.702
Well, for one, on the website,

00:16:43.702 --> 00:16:46.238
there is a list of a
slightly vague commitment

00:16:46.238 --> 00:16:48.707
to removing all artificial
colors, flavors,

00:16:48.707 --> 00:16:50.409
and preservatives from their fried chicken

00:16:50.409 --> 00:16:52.244
by the end of 2022.

00:16:52.244 --> 00:16:54.646
So, that's this year,
guys. Better get on it.

00:16:54.646 --> 00:16:55.748
Also by the end of this year,

00:16:55.748 --> 00:16:59.118
they want to remove all
MSG from their chicken.

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.619
Now, correct me if I'm wrong,

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:01.820
but that implies they currently

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.922
are using MSG on the chicken.

00:17:03.922 --> 00:17:06.191
But how much and to which chicken dishes

00:17:06.191 --> 00:17:07.659
they're actually adding MSG,

00:17:07.659 --> 00:17:09.328
they have not specified.

00:17:09.328 --> 00:17:11.430
They also want to use only cage-free eggs

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.999
by the end of 2025.

00:17:13.999 --> 00:17:15.968
Take your time there, guys, jeez.

00:17:15.968 --> 00:17:18.470
Also, cage-free "eggs"?

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.072
What about the chickens?

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:21.507
One interesting thing is that in the UK,

00:17:21.507 --> 00:17:23.308
Popeyes has pledged to
make all its chicken halal,

00:17:23.308 --> 00:17:25.210
meaning it's suitable
for Muslim people to eat.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.880
Popeyes UK also uses Red
Tractor-assured chicken.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.181
This is a farming standards board

00:17:29.181 --> 00:17:31.383
which oversees poultry farming in the UK.

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:32.418
To be Red Tractor-assured,

00:17:32.418 --> 00:17:34.520
you can't do things like
wash your chicken in chlorine

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.088
or use antibiotics on your chicken,

00:17:36.088 --> 00:17:39.024
unless it's approved by a vet
to treat a specific illness.

00:17:39.024 --> 00:17:41.160
Red Tractor doesn't exist in the US,

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.262
but Popeyes does say it uses chicken

00:17:43.262 --> 00:17:46.098
free from added hormones and steroids.

00:17:46.098 --> 00:17:47.900
There's a commitment on Popeyes' website

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.169
to removing antibiotics from its chickens

00:17:50.169 --> 00:17:51.570
by the end of 2021.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.638
So that's right around the corner

00:17:52.638 --> 00:17:53.705
at the time of recording this,

00:17:53.705 --> 00:17:56.175
and we reached out to them
for what was going on,

00:17:56.175 --> 00:17:58.710
and they told us X, [laughs]

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.046
which is code for nothing.

00:18:01.046 --> 00:18:02.714
Red Tractor certification also means

00:18:02.714 --> 00:18:04.817
that chickens must be kept
in a safe, comfortable,

00:18:04.817 --> 00:18:06.952
hygienic, and sufficiently sized housing;

00:18:06.952 --> 00:18:08.654
given a full, healthy diet;

00:18:08.654 --> 00:18:11.090
and have permanent access
to environmental enrichment

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.658
that is suitable for their needs.

00:18:12.658 --> 00:18:14.626
Again, we do not have
Red Tractor in the US,

00:18:14.626 --> 00:18:16.728
but Popeyes claims it wants to, quote,

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:18.864
"promote practices that support

00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:21.066
and address the globally recognized

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:24.203
five freedoms of animal
welfare," end quote.

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:26.271
These principles broadly line up

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:29.241
with the Red Tractor
guarantees, which are:

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:30.909
freedom from hunger and thirst,

00:18:30.909 --> 00:18:32.511
freedom from discomfort,

00:18:32.511 --> 00:18:34.413
freedom from pain, injury, and disease,

00:18:34.413 --> 00:18:36.748
freedom to express
normal, natural behaviors,

00:18:36.748 --> 00:18:39.551
like accommodating for
chickens' instinct to roost,

00:18:39.551 --> 00:18:42.187
and freedom from fear and distress.

00:18:42.187 --> 00:18:44.256
I don't even get those freedoms!

00:18:44.256 --> 00:18:45.390
I'm terrified all the time!

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:46.225
[chicken clucks]

00:18:46.225 --> 00:18:48.927
So it looks like they're aiming
for equivalent standards,

00:18:48.927 --> 00:18:52.030
even if they don't have
a nice Red Tractor badge

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:54.266
or whatever to prove
that they've achieved it.

00:18:54.266 --> 00:18:56.802
Now, obviously Popeyes is a
Louisiana fast-food chain.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.737
Joe asked me to try and
find Louisiana on a map.

00:18:58.737 --> 00:19:00.205
I don't know much about
American geography.

00:19:00.205 --> 00:19:02.741
I can tell you where California is,

00:19:02.741 --> 00:19:05.777
where Texas is, where Florida is.

00:19:05.777 --> 00:19:07.880
New York is somewhere over here, I think.

00:19:08.881 --> 00:19:11.817
If I had to hazard a guess
as to where Louisiana was,

00:19:11.817 --> 00:19:13.252
I mean, it's the South, right?

00:19:13.252 --> 00:19:14.253
It's the South.

00:19:14.253 --> 00:19:15.354
Maybe ...

00:19:16.622 --> 00:19:18.757
is it, like, this one?

00:19:18.757 --> 00:19:20.225
Maybe that one there.

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.461
♪ "Wars" in this house ♪

00:19:22.461 --> 00:19:24.730
There's "Food Wars" in this house

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.964
"Wars" in this house

00:19:25.964 --> 00:19:27.533
There's "Food Wars" in this house ♪

